		<label>Grax</label>
		<description>Graxes are representatives of flint life on this planet. They are quite rare and close to extinction. Most often you can see them near thermal springs on volcanic fields, where they can lie dormant for many years.
Grax metabolism is designed in a special way. For digestion, they need to consume sulfur, which is involved in the synthesis of sulfuric and silicic acid. They have a respiratory system to obtain oxygen. The main source of energy is the sun, the absence of which is deadly. Being in a hot place can partially cover the need for sunlight.
Grax are a little-studied species, but they are most often described as aggressive and rude, sleepy and intelligent creatures. The xenos civilization is at a primitive level, but they have high potential due to the structure of the nervous system.
Military biologists recommend not disturbing the sleep of these creatures, but if this does happen, it is worth using explosives or blunt weapons to split the natural armor.</description>
